--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Multi-argument std::function construction and call in C++17 mode.  Layer-1
partial-spec pack deduction (cpp11_partial_spec_pack_after_fixed), the member
function-pointer pack-arity collapse (cpp11_variadic_pack_in_member_funptr_type)
and the method-body pack-expansion use (cpp11_variadic_pack_in_method_body_call)
are all fixed, so the converting constructor resolves, wires up _M_invoker /
_M_manager with the correct arity, and operator() forwards both arguments
correctly.  The remaining gap is deeper in the dispatch chain
(_Function_handler::_M_invoke -> std::__invoke_r -> __invoke_impl): the
invocation yields a wrong result (returns 1 instead of 5 for add(2,3)) although
the operator()-level argument forwarding is correct.  Single-argument
std::function invokes correctly and soundly (N5008 [func.wrap.func],
[temp.variadic]/5).  Previously this test passed only VACUOUSLY.  Flip to CORE
once the multi-argument invoke/__invoke_r dispatch returns the correct result.
